# How do you save a lost game?
teaches: ["endgames/saving-lost-games"]
voices: {"a":"gemini:Charon | calm, warm chess coach","b":"gemini:Puck | eager club player, relaxed and good-humoured; never exaggerated"}
prompt: "How do stalemate tricks and perpetual check save half a point? What is a fortress, and how do you make the opponent prove it?"
next: {"title":"How do you think with the clock running?","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/chess-30-days/28-how-do-you-think-with-the-clock-running.cast"}

## Warm-up: mate, and the stalemate trap
use: chess_board
with:
    positions:
      - {fen: 3r2k1/p4ppp/1q6/8/8/8/P2Q1PPP/3R2K1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Qxd8+, Qxd8, Rxd8#]}
      - {fen: 8/8/8/1p6/1Q6/8/p1K5/k7 w - - 0 1, moves: [Qxb5]}
      - {fen: 8/8/8/1p6/1Q6/8/p1K5/k7 w - - 0 1, moves: [Qb2#]}
    position_shown: 0
    plies_shown: 0

    card title Warm-up

A: Today the tables turn: how do you save a game you're losing? First, two warm-ups.
    draw position

B: Black's queen is aiming at f2. I'd guard it first.
    highlight piece_b6

A: Before you guard f2, the Three Questions: your own checks first.
    point at.ref piece_f2 gesture circle

    pause 0.3

    ask "Win the game." widget chess line true hints ["His back rank has no air, and his rook on d8 has one guard.","Your queen and rook stand in a line on the d-file."] themes ["back rank"] voice a teaches ["safety/back-rank"]
        right: Queen takes d8, check. The queen takes back, and your rook takes on d8: mate on the back rank.
        wrong: Checks first. Which check takes away his rook's only guard?

B: A whole queen, for mate. Cheap.
    point at.ref piece_g8 gesture circle

A: Now an ending like last time's. You're a queen up, and it's your move.
    animate position_shown 1 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

B: Easy. Take the b-pawn, then mate him.
    animate plies_shown 1 duration 1.3

A: Look at his king now: no square, and his last pawn can't move. No legal move, no check: stalemate, a draw.
    highlight piece_a1

A: Back one move. This time, finish it.
    animate position_shown 2 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

    pause 0.3

    ask "Finish it." widget chess line true hints ["Leave his pawn alone.","A check his king can't escape."] themes ["conversion","stalemate"] voice a teaches ["endgames/conversion","endgames/saving-lost-games"]
        right: Checkmate. Queen to b2 mates, guarded by your king; e1, c3 or d4 mate too. Taking the pawn was stalemate.
        wrong: If you take the pawn, he has no move at all. Is there a check instead?

B: So the winner has to watch out for stalemate.
    highlight piece_a1

A: And today you're on the losing side, hoping he does exactly that.
    animate position_shown 1 plies_shown 1 duration 0.6

## Three ways to save half a point
use: chess_board
with:
    positions:
      - {fen: 2Q5/5Rpk/8/1p2p1qp/1P2Pn1P/5PP1/4r3/7K b - - 2 48, moves: [Qxg3, Qg8+, Kxg8, Rxg7+, Kxg7]}
      - {fen: 2Q5/5Rpk/8/1p2p2p/1P2Pn1P/5Pq1/4r3/7K w - - 0 49, moves: [Rxg7+, Kxg7]}
      - {fen: 6k1/6R1/8/1p2p2p/1P2Pn1P/5Pq1/4r3/7K b - - 0 50, moves: [Kh8, Rh7+, Kg8, Rg7+]}
      - {fen: 8/7k/6pp/8/2Q5/8/1r2q3/7K w - - 0 1, moves: [Qxe2, Rxe2]}
      - {fen: 8/7k/6pp/8/2Q5/8/1r2q3/7K w - - 0 1, moves: [Qf7+, Kh8, Qf8+, Kh7, Qf7+]}
      - {fen: 7k/8/5K2/7P/8/3B4/8/8 w - - 0 1, moves: [Kg6, Kg8, h6, Kh8, h7], highlights: [h8]}
      - {fen: 7k/2B5/6KP/8/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1, moves: [Be5+, Kg8, h7+, Kf8, h8=Q+], highlights: [h8]}
    position_shown: 0
    plies_shown: 0
sources:
    - id: swindle
      title: Swindle (chess)
      authors: Wikipedia contributors
      year: 2026
      finding: 'Evans–Reshevsky, US Championship 1963–64: 47.h4! Re2+ 48.Kh1 Qxg3?? 49.Qg8+! Kxg8 50.Rxg7+! ½–½ — taking the rook is stalemate, otherwise the rook keeps checking; dubbed the ''Swindle of the Century''.'
      url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swindle_(chess)
    - id: tablebase
      title: Lichess endgame tablebase
      authors: Lichess
      year: 2026
      finding: The perpetual (Qf7+/Qf8+), the light-bishop h-pawn fortress (draw) and the dark-bishop version (White wins) were checked in the 7-piece tablebase.
      url: https://tablebase.lichess.ovh

    card title "Three rescues"

A: Now you're the one who's lost. A famous case: Evans against Reshevsky, at the US Championship of 1963 to 64.
    draw position

B: White is a knight down for a pawn. I'd have resigned ages ago.
    highlight piece_f4

A: Larry Evans played on. Reshevsky, winning, grabbed a pawn with his queen.
    animate plies_shown 1 duration 1.3

A: Look at White's king: it has no square, and every White pawn is blocked.
    highlight piece_h1 piece_b4 piece_e4 piece_f3 piece_h4

    animate position_shown 1 plies_shown 0 duration 0.01

B: So I check. Rook takes g7!
    animate plies_shown 1 duration 1.3

A: The king takes, and you still have a queen that can move. Black wins.
    animate plies_shown 2 duration 1.3

    animate position_shown 0 plies_shown 1 duration 0.4

    pause 0.3

    ask "Save the game." widget chess line 2 hints ["Your king and pawns can't move. What if nothing else of yours could move either?","Give your queen away, with check."] themes ["stalemate"] voice a
        right: Queen to g8, check: take it, or be mated. He takes.
        wrong: Which check gets rid of your queen?

A: Then rook takes g7, check. Take the rook, and White has no legal move and no check: stalemate, a draw.
    blocking false

    animate plies_shown 4 duration 1.3

    pause 1.2

    animate plies_shown 5 duration 1.3

    highlight piece_h1

    animate position_shown 2 plies_shown 0 duration 0.01

A: Run from the rook, and it follows: check after check.
    blocking false

    animate plies_shown 1 duration 1.2

    animate plies_shown 2 duration 1.2

    animate plies_shown 4 duration 2

A: They agreed a draw: the swindle of the century, people called it.
    highlight piece_g7

A: So here's the test: your king and pawns can't move? Then give everything else away, with check.
    highlight piece_h1

A: Second rescue. White is a rook and two pawns down, and Black t (@highlight piece_e2@)hreatens queen to f1, mate.
    blocking false

    animate position_shown 3 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

B: Queen takes queen!
    animate plies_shown 1 duration 1.3

A: The rook takes back, and you have nothing left but your king.
    animate plies_shown 2 duration 1.3

    animate position_shown 4 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

    pause 0.3

    ask "Save the game." widget chess line true hints ["Checks first: is there one his king can't run from?","f7, then f8."] themes ["perpetual check"] voice a
        right: Queen to f7, check: the king's only square is h8. Queen to f8, check: back to h7. Then f7 again.
        wrong: Look at every check, and where his king can go after each.

A: Round and round: the same position three times is a draw. That's perpetual check.
    highlight piece_f7

A: The last rescue needs no checks at all. Whi (@highlight piece_d3 piece_h5@)te is a bishop and a pawn up.
    blocking false

    animate position_shown 5 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

B: An easy win. King to g6, then push the pawn.
    animate plies_shown 1 duration 1.3

A: Black's king steps to g8, and back to h8 when the pawn comes.
    animate plies_shown 4 duration 3

B: Pawn to h7.
    animate plies_shown 5 duration 1.3

A: Stalemate. And h8 is a dark square: this bishop can never touch it, so it never drives the king out.
    draw hl_h8

A: That's a fortress. You sit in it, and make him prove the win.
    highlight piece_h8

A: Now a bishop on dark squares, and the pawn on h6. Can Black still hold the corner?
    animate position_shown 6 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

    quiz "With a dark-squared bishop, can Black still hold the corner?" on_canvas true voice a
        right: No. h8 is dark, so this bishop takes the corner away and the king is driven out. The wrong bishop draws, the right one wins.
        wrong: What colour is the queening square?
        * Yes: the corner holds
        + No: the bishop covers h8
        * Only with Black to move

A: No: h8 is dark. The bishop checks from e5, the king has to leave the corner, and the pawn queens.
    blocking false

    animate plies_shown 1 duration 1.2

    animate plies_shown 2 duration 1.2

    animate plies_shown 5 duration 2.4

    hide position hl_h8

A: Stalemate, perpetual, fortress: when you're lost, look for one before you resign.
    text c_stale "stalemate" x 500 y 470 font_size 56
    text c_perp "perpetual" x 500 y 385 font_size 56
    text c_fort "fortress" x 500 y 300 font_size 56
    parallel true

## Your turn: save it
feedback:
    style: dry
    perfect: Four for four. You'll be hard to beat, even when you're lost.
    good: Most of them. The rescues you missed will come round again.
    poor: Saving games is a new habit. These come back until they stick.
    none: The positions will wait for you.
use: chess_board
with:
    positions:
      - {fen: 7k/5Q1p/7P/2q5/8/8/6PP/5R1K b - - 0 1, moves: [Qg1+, Rxg1], flip: true}
      - {fen: 4k3/8/4K2P/8/8/8/8/5B2 b - - 0 1, moves: [Kf8], flip: true}
      - {fen: k7/2Q5/8/8/8/6r1/8/6K1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Qxg3]}
      - {fen: 6k1/6p1/8/1Q6/3q4/8/1r6/7K w - - 0 1, moves: [Qe8+, Kh7]}
      - {fen: 4Q3/6pk/8/8/3q4/8/1r6/7K w - - 2 2}
      - {fen: k7/2Q5/8/8/8/6r1/8/6K1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Kh2, Rh3+, Kxh3]}
    position_shown: 0
    plies_shown: 0

    card title "Your turn"

A: Now you've seen three rescues: your turn. Four positions, then a game to save against the computer.
    draw position

A: First, you're Black, so the board has turned. White threatens queen to g7, mate.
    highlight piece_f7

    pause 0.3

    ask "Save the game." widget chess line true hints ["Your king can't move, and your pawn is blocked.","Give your queen away, with check."] themes ["stalemate"] voice a test save
        right: Queen to g1, check. The rook takes it, and you have no legal move left: stalemate.
        wrong: Your king has no move. What if your queen were gone too?

B: The Evans trick, in miniature.
    highlight piece_h8

A: Black again, and a review of today's fortress: find the only move that holds.
    animate position_shown 1 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

    pause 0.3

    ask "Hold the draw." widget chess line true hints ["Where does the pawn queen, and what colour is that square?","Head for the corner."] themes ["defence"] voice a test save
        right: King to f8, heading for g8 and h8: the dark corner this bishop can never touch.
        wrong: Which corner can a light-squared bishop never attack?

A: Now you're White and winning, and the board turns back. Black's rook has just checked you.
    animate position_shown 2 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

    animate position_shown 5 plies_shown 0 duration 0.01

B: I'll step my king to h2, out of the check.
    animate plies_shown 1 duration 1.3

A: Then the rook checks again. Take it with your king, and his boxed-in king has no move: stalemate.
    blocking false

    animate plies_shown 2 duration 1.3

    pause 0.8

    animate plies_shown 3 duration 1.3

    highlight piece_a8

A: Back to the check. You can do better.
    animate position_shown 2 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

    pause 0.3

    ask "Deal with the check." widget chess line true hints ["His king is boxed in. Count its squares after each of your moves.","Your queen."] themes ["conversion","stalemate"] voice a test save teaches ["endgames/conversion","endgames/saving-lost-games"]
        right: Queen takes g3. Your queen leaves c7, so his king gets a7 and b7: no stalemate, and it's a queen against nothing.
        wrong: A king move still wins, but slowly: the rook keeps checking. Find the quickest way.

A: Last one, a new pattern. You're a rook and a pawn down, and Black threatens mate on your back rank.
    animate position_shown 3 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

    pause 0.3

    ask "Save the game." widget chess line true hints ["Checks first.","The e-file is open."] themes ["perpetual check"] voice a test save
        right: Queen to e8, check. The king's only square is h7.
        wrong: Find a check his king can't run from.

    hide position

A: You scored {save.score} of {save.total}.
    results test save

    show position

A: Now keep that one going, against the computer. It will try to escape the checks.
    animate position_shown 4 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

A: Hold for fifteen moves, or until the position repeats.
    explore activity vs_computer goal.kind hold goal.within 15 store hold

    hide position

A: Lost isn't over. King and pawns stuck? Give everything else away, with check.
    text c_stale "stalemate" x 500 y 470 font_size 56

A: His king in the open? Check it, and keep checking.
    text c_perp "perpetual" x 500 y 385 font_size 56

A: A wall he can't break? Sit behind it, and make him prove the win.
    text c_fort "fortress" x 500 y 300 font_size 56

    erase c_stale c_perp c_fort

A: Homework: one slow game today, fifteen plus ten or slower.
    text hw "15 + 10" x 500 y 440 font_size 64

A: Then find its first mistake.
    text hw2 "1st mistake?" x 500 y 330 font_size 64

## Where next
end_page: true

